<title>USA: TABLE - BNCCORP Inc Q2 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BNCCORP Inc Q2 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>BISMARCK, N.D. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>For Q2 Ended     For 6 Months Ended</p>
<p>				  June 30	     June 30</p>
<p>			     1997	1996	   1997	1996</p>
<p>Interest income	 $6,426    $5,012	 $12,486    $9,497</p>
<p>Interest expense	 3,337     2,670	   6,452     5,207</p>
<p>Net interest income    3,089     2,342	   6,034     4,290</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>    loan losses	  2,083	 135	   2,253	 219</p>
<p>Noninterest income	 465	 521	     946	 892</p>
<p>Noninterest expense    2,349     2,056	   4,689     4,022</p>
<p>Net income		  (568)	439		(7)	581</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per</p>
<p>    common share	($0.24)    $0.19	  ($0.00)    $0.25</p>
<p>Assets		  $304,862  $249,891	$299,456  $243,222</p>
<p>NOTE: As previously reported, Q2 1997 loss after one-time, extraordinary $1.9 million increase in loan loss provision, allegedly resulting from questionable loan practices by a recently dismissed employee. Excluding provision, Q2 1997 net income would have been $663,000 or $0.28 a share.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
